  "testId": "testClasses.webstore.getAnAccount.RegistrationAndLoginTest#verifyRegistrationFunctionality",
  "scenario": {
    "summary": "Guest opens Create Account, checks the empty-form validation messages and field labels, registers a new account (username = e-mail = date+time+sheet suffix), checks HELLO, reads the username in My Profile, logs off, then tries to register the same username again and checks the duplicate-user message.",
    "steps": [
      "Open the webstore, Login, Create Account",
      "Submit the empty form, verify the four validation messages",
      "Verify the four field labels",
      "Register with username/e-mail = date + time + sheet suffix and the sheet password",
      "Verify My Account link and 'HELLO'",
      "Open My Profile, read the username, log off",
      "Register again with the same username, verify the duplicate-user message"
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "user"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [
      "Creates a NEW registered account on the store per run (username = e-mail built from CUSTOM_DATE + CURRENT_TIME + sheet suffix); no cleanup, one account left per run (no ledger undo)"
    ],
    "assertions": [
      "Validation messages and labels",
      "Greeting 'HELLO'",
      "Duplicate username message (centralizedLoginEnabled=no) or the new message box (yes)"
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "No need: the account is created by the test. loginAndRegistration!F7 (Username/Input, masked) is only the suffix of the generated username -> created-by-test; F9/F10 (Password/ConfirmPassword Input, masked) are the password the test sets on the new account -> created-by-test (same as the approved Playwright create-account entry). The second registration reuses the username the test just created (read from My Profile).",
      "Masked labels/messages, not credentials: B7..B10 (field labels) and C7..C10 (validation messages) are masked only because the key names contain username/email/password -> expected-output.",
      "REVIEW: each run leaves a new registered account on MaxwellsHardware; cleanup would need an admin-side delete (out of TDA scope).",
      "Store: openWebstoreUrl opens automation_webStoreUrl (atstage: webstore-z10-atstage, the main store MaxwellsHardware), the same store as the Selenium pdp/quickOrder/plp entries.",
      "Profile: work/profiles/profile.json has no observations for these Selenium cells (profiled false); DB facts from bin/tda rows (2026-11-11) where cited.",
      "Scanned constant values (locators, report messages, map keys, image paths) are framework constants: role config, no need.",
      "migrate: Selenium reads Excel tables through TestData.getMap / getHashMap; there is no swap for Selenium."
    ],
    "confidence": "high",
    "needsReview": true
  },
